<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89a72fa638fd2a23c47b7d983ac145b454a4ff3f08bc19a85a6bb126e4544b24</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What Earth's sixth mass extinction event means for humans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e88f2293ecfe8d68ac58a288830bc332bcf5988e24bfe0798390ca14e6d9325</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410--0a12d110aea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human activity is driving plants and animals to extinction at an unprecedented rate. As countries meet in Armenia to discuss ways to reverse nature loss, DW reveals how declining biodiversity is already harming people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>France: Young voters blase about Glucksmann's Socialists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0c74ee2686bd5622851cbe7450eac76fac49e1d60e47145b2131f09dd65c8a0</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159--5c98176d41f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Raphael Glucksmann wants to lead France's Socialists to power without working with the left-populist Jean-Luc Melenchon, who is particularly popular with young voters. How can the center-left candidate win them over?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How reliant is Ukraine on the US-controlled Starlink internet service?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a60cbbdcdbd74ad98314e4977e46ae7dbfa722d7035a8d0e7032a4103192b16</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729--6217d664b01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kyiv keeps issuing warnings that the satellite internet system Starlink is being restricted in Ukraine. How dependent is the country on the system, and what would happen if it went down?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Populist Czech PM Babis goes empty-handed in Senate elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfe8a62913042f7c856eeef4baa0d39cbe7d96186f18d063bfa8e0aa0feb9e54</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934--95037aa1aa28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/populist-czech-pm-babis-goes-empty-handed-in-senate-elections/a-79690934?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties still control the Czech Senate, in a major blow to Prime Minister Andrej Babis' and his governing coalition.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50c47c3e659ddb5eab18df7630888a368e71e780288d2ae055a5744d628bc1bf</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703--c66cb23b1a91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy says Russia is trying to cut electricity and heating to civilians ahead of winter. He also called the US president's waiver of new sanctions on Moscow a boost for Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Protesters clash with police in nationwide protests, amid rising social polarization</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5640175577c2d632eaa49dbb43905446d15f255cf9aaf15a7e26fd6173eb4a10</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584--b410e6f9b726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Unrest broke out in parts of France as students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists took to the streets to protest high prices and inequality. Police arrested over 1,000 people amid chaotic scenes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e83cd9bbd88578a113392223db031e408ece08ea7455ca51317b3bc82aa341</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d22f518e7985b7ad375c0bacc21c4bf9f63e49038f3a6a34403f73440b6419f2</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39408d18bb364063cad853550dde1c9cd4c72bdfa244ecb452951a9b22018067</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95933806ef3eea31981883fdb4d0040d5a29fc6ac3418bc7ecf9e5bcc0b2dc46</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8593072d297a85eeab6099c9c09735a64a66b52e55f2e00595e651cca60f7dc6</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133--8d0677d89358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing problems with the data transmission network, Italian authorities have drastically reduced the volume of flights in their airspace. The ENAV authority ruled out malicious activity and said flights remained safe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Police raid the major pro-opposition Halk TV channel in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83d7b45f0713ae6517ed4fe5f7a0fad78b238370782e0c2fef59c06e1538a449</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673--402c2b295200.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish police raided the Istanbul headquarters of an important pro-opposition television station on Wednesdazy, the day that jailed Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu was set to start his defense against corruption charges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU summit to focus on China, Ukraine and bloc budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f7aa7649fc7e1f9deee45483124196464705cb088c52ca20d161ad9c6766e91</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338--d6856904c849.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders meeting in Brussels will examine measures to curb the bloc's huge trade deficit with China. But they will also be looking to further agreement on the next EU budget ahead of some major elections next year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Romania: 2 ships on fire in Black Sea, 7 crew missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16c4b52d817336bcc47b62e8fd05b7355a4905b3d927bd53cab2207d9c3dc9b9</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003--b330bc2c57d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two chemical tankers have caught fire in Romanian territorial waters in the Black Sea. The blazes occurred after Russian drones were sighted in Romanian airspace.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Fire at Education Ministry as students protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9aa4ea0531d39dadd766e42477b0f78ac3fc48e6ecd63c89daae99941dd5e1d</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-fire-at-education-ministry-as-students-protest/a-79661193--fb85f85aef8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-fire-at-education-ministry-as-students-protest/a-79661193?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Riot police deployed in the Albanian capital Tirana on the second day of student protests. The sudden outbreak seemed at least somewhat reminiscent of the widespread demos in France courting international attention.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading graph about alleged Russian bot activity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51ccd752cc3e1c5b5717d979dfff06273c902ba547d9d241b8b654ccb672d23a</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-graph-about-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769--ec259de6b65a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-graph-about-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Did attacks on Russian data centers reduce bot activity around Germany's AfD? A viral graph claims they did. But it contains significant inconsistencies and provides no evidence to support the claim.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine allies in Poland after Starlink sabotage, Trump diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58683faf5e9caecff6ece8005c13122de5f9a7dfea008301a9754d43a2ef51a5</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-allies-in-poland-after-starlink-sabotage-trump-diesel-deal/a-79653869--c0d0565fa8d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-allies-in-poland-after-starlink-sabotage-trump-diesel-deal/a-79653869?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's Johann Wadephul said hybrid plots like the Starlink fire showed Europe was "in Russia's crosshairs." The UK's Ed Miliband said Trump's Russian diesel deal led to a "very difficult few days" diplomatically.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and the US: What's next after Trump's diesel deal with Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b1dd32a20f376bf5e8b95ec1f30afea3659879549949e0afece3358d32bda11</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T18:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-the-us-what-s-next-after-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia/a-79650785--59d833db4bc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-the-us-what-s-next-after-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia/a-79650785?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump plans to allow the purchase of Russian diesel, drawing criticism at home and abroad. What is behind the US president's decision and what should Ukraine do next? DW spoke with experts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Critics warn of espionage risks as Slovakia restores military-diplomatic representation with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e3b595bc2a103616a1fc30431b7d935cf4b600c211cfdc017577ecc1d64bf79</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641--99619951a602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovakia is restoring military-diplomatic relations with Russia for the first time since 2022. The government has defended the move but critics warn of espionage risks and further damage to trust within NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
